content.text:
Three failures now reproduce through the real built CLI:

- a linked worktree backed by `--separate-git-dir …/.git` installs hooks at the storage directory’s `.codex/hooks.json`, outside either checkout;
- a primary checkout whose `.codex` directory is a symlink causes linked-worktree enablement to write hooks into the symlink target;
- a symlinked `.codex/hooks.json` is silently replaced by a regular file during `enable --force`.

These are concrete filesystem-boundary and configuration-integrity regressions. I’m still completing the full unit/integration/canary suite so the final verdict separates “tests pass” from “behavior is safe.”

